Description:The present invention provides a system and method for automatically identifying software refactoring opportunities within a Java codebase. Through static code analysis, machine learning, and predefined refactoring patterns, the system detects code smells, generates actionable suggestions, and prioritizes refactoring tasks to improve code maintainability, readability, and performance. The system integrates with development environments to provide real-time feedback, thereby enhancing developer productivity and reducing the risk of errors , C , C , Claims:1. A system for automatically identifying refactoring opportunities in a Java codebase, comprising:
• A code analysis module configured to perform static code analysis on the Java codebase;
• A refactoring opportunity detection engine configured to identify potential refactoring opportunities based on predefined patterns and machine learning models;
• A refactoring suggestions generator configured to generate actionable refactoring suggestions;
• A user interface for displaying the refactoring suggestions to developers.
2. The system of claim 1, wherein the code analysis module computes code metrics such as cyclomatic complexity, class coupling, and code duplication to identify potential refactoring opportunities.
3. The system of claim 1, wherein the refactoring opportunity detection engine applies machine learning models to predict which areas of the codebase would benefit most from refactoring.
4. A method for automatically identifying software refactoring opportunities in a Java codebase, comprising:
• Analyzing the Java codebase using static code analysis to extract relevant code metrics;
• Applying predefined refactoring patterns to detect areas that require refactoring;
• Generating refactoring suggestions based on the identified opportunities;
